   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 7.2. Increased capacity of member States to ensure safe and healthy working conditions</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">In August 2020, the Ministry of Health (MOH); Ministry of Mines and Minerals
Development (MMMD); Federation of Free Trade
Unions of Zambia (FFFTUZ); Lusaka City Council (LCC); Occupational Health and Safety Institute (OHSI); Zambia Congress of Trade Unions (ZCTU); and Zambia Federation of Employers (ZFE) developed and adopted an OSH Workplace COVID19 and OSH Guidelines by government in collaboration with social partners. The implementation of the programme is in progress.  The national OSH policy awaits Cabinet approval. The ILO convened 2 virtual tripartite consultations in June and July 2020 discussing the development of the COVID-19 workplace policy guidelines and undertook a normative review of the final version of the guidelines. The approved OSH workplace safety and health guidelines for Zambia incorporate the changes based on the ILO comments and feedback.</narrative>
   </description>
